   Renaming a custom provider deletes the old provider key but does not migrate separately saved models whose `provider` field still contains the old name. Those models then resolve no credential and stop working.
   ```tsx
   			await storage.customProviders.set(provider as any);
   			const oldName = dialog.provider?.name;
   			if (oldName && oldName !== provider.name) {
   				await storage.providerKeys.delete(oldName);
   			}
   			if (form.apiKey.trim()) {
   				await storage.providerKeys.set(provider.name, form.apiKey.trim());
   			} else {
   				await storage.providerKeys.delete(provider.name);
   			}
   ```

2. `logic_error` — severity 3, confidence 0.99  
   Location: `web/src/keating/ui-settings.ts:182`  
   The v3 migration treats every old stored `0` as an automatic default. A user who explicitly turned comparisons off under schema v2 is silently re-enabled at 1%, contradicting the comment’s claim that explicit choices are preserved.
   ```ts
   		alternativeResponseChance:
   			value?.schemaVersion !== UI_SETTINGS_SCHEMA_VERSION
   				&& (value?.alternativeResponseChance === 0.05 || value?.alternativeResponseChance === 0)
   				? DEFAULT_UI_SETTINGS.alternativeResponseChance
   				: normalizeAlternativeResponseChance(value?.alternativeResponseChance),
   ```

3. `logic_error` — severity 2, confidence 0.96  
   Location: `web/src/components/settings/MyModelsSection.tsx:232`  
   Selecting a custom provider fills its API type and base URL, but switching back to a built-in provider retains those custom values. Saving then creates, for example, an `openai` model pointed at the previous custom endpoint.
   ```tsx
   							onChange={(e) => {
   								const providerName = e.target.value;
   								const customProvider = customProviders.find((provider) => provider.name === providerName);
   								dispatch({
   									type: "change",
   									form: {
   										...modelForm,
   										provider: providerName,
   										api: customProvider ? providerApi(customProvider) : modelForm.api,
   										baseUrl: customProvider?.baseUrl ?? modelForm.baseUrl,
   									},
   								});
   							}}
   ```

4. `incomplete_integration_with_existing_code` — severity 2, confidence 0.99  
   Location: `web/src/pages/Tutorial.tsx:615`  
   `ProxyTab` removes the toggle and proxy URL controls, but the tutorial still instructs users to use those now-nonexistent controls.
   ```tsx
   								A CORS proxy lets this browser-based app call providers that block direct
   								cross-origin requests. Toggle <strong>Use CORS Proxy</strong> and set the{" "}
   								<strong>Proxy URL</strong> (e.g.{" "}
